% PowerPoint slides 6.
### Eliminating Ambiguity
[intro] @(84, 165) {$body} Change the grammar so these operators {{color=emp|associate left}}.
[oldhead] @(84, 252) {$body, w=520px, color=id} Original grammar
[newhead] @(690, 252) {$body, w=520px, color=emp} Revised grammar
@(84, 310) {$code, size=26px} ```
Start → Expr
Expr → Expr Op Expr
Expr → Int
Expr → Open Expr Close
```
...
@(690, 310) {$code, size=26px} ```
Start → Expr
Expr → Expr Op Term
Expr → Term
Term → Int
Term → Open Expr Close
```
...
[why] @(84, 584) {$note} The right operand is a {{color=emp|Term}}. An unparenthesized operator sequence can only grow on the left.
% Lecture 5 used Num for this role; Lecture 6 calls it Term.
---
