% PowerPoint slides 32.
### Statement Parsing
@(84, 156) {$code, w=1112px, size=24px} ```cpp
ASTNode ParseStatement() {
  if (lexer.None()) Error("Expected Statement.");

  using namespace emplex;
  switch (lexer.Peek()) {
    case Lexer::ID_VAR:   return ParseStatement_Var();
    case Lexer::ID_IF:    return ParseStatement_If();
    case Lexer::ID_WHILE: return ParseStatement_While();
    case Lexer::ID_PRINT: return ParseStatement_Print();
    case '{':            return ParseStatement_Block();
    // List other statement starts here...
    default:             return ParseStatement_Expression();
  }
}
```
...
[why] @(84, 665) {$note} The lookahead selects a procedure that returns an {{color=emp|AST node}}.
% At the program entry point, also require EOF after the complete parse.
% Lexer::ID_* and ASTNode retain the course-specific interfaces from the source.
